      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we add a shared type alias in `neard_dbus.hpp` then it will be available in `fru_device.cpp` as well and it will not be clear which code depends on the interface definition.\n\nPreviously maintainers mentioned to me that being able to find usages of D-Bus  interfaces in source code is important to them. I agree with that sentiment therefore i will keep these type aliases in the source files where they are used.\n\nOtherwise finding where interfaces are used would involve tracking down type aliases through multiple files.\n\nFor a non PDI type alias that we define ourselves i would agree with you that it could be part of a shared header and should be defined once. This is a different matter since the alias is always the same and commonly defined this way in various repositories.\n\nIf you want to work on this direction i would recommend you to define macros in the PDI generated headers to provide these type aliases so we don\u0027t have to define them ourselves. Similar to `PHOSPHOR_LOG2_USING`.",
